Enums in :mod:`icalendar.enums` accept values in any case, so ``icalendar.enums.PARTSTAT("needs-action")`` is :attr:`icalendar.enums.PARTSTAT.NEEDS_ACTION`. Enumerated property values and property parameter values that are not enclosed in double quotes are case-insensitive per :rfc:`5545#section-3.1`. Reading a calendar with a lower-case value, such as ``STATUS:confirmed``, no longer raises :exc:`ValueError`.
